BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dining Out For Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T235900
UID:8079b9b76cb55e7726669c79eda47039@growthzone.com
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for Food For Thought’s 25th annual fundraiser\, Di
 ning Out For Life on Thursday\, December 3! Dining Out For Life is Sonoma 
 County's largest dine and donate event\, with over 60 participating locati
 ons—ranging from cozy coffee shops to beloved casual and fine dining spo
 ts. Each location is donating a percentage of sales to provide healthy foo
 d and loving support to thousands of our neighbors in need. Plus\, patrons
  and donors have a chance to win one of 9 drawing prizes\, including a 7-n
 ight stay in Mexico and packages from Oliver’s Market\, Glen Ellen Star\
 , Rotten Robbie\, River Electric\, The Junction Beer Garden\, and other lo
 cal restaurants. Dine Out and Take Out on December 3 to Give Back. Find yo
 ur flavor at FFTfoodbank.org/DOFL. Healdsburg Locations: Acre Pizza Baci C
 afé & Wine Bar Drewish Deli Lo & Behold Bar + Kitchen Spoonbar Windsor Lo
 cations: Himalayan Restaurant Machado Burgers Qimura Sushi & Ramen Russian
  River Brewing Company Sweet T’s Restaurant + Bar Umé Japanese Bist
URL:https://business.petalumachamber.com/events/details/dining-out-for-lif
 e-12-03-2026
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winter’s Night\, Winter Choral Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261206T180000
UID:9c724d01bb91bd7b6426788a307a4be5@growthzone.com
DESCRIPTION:Our very own Petaluma Women’s Chorus presents the shimmering
  sounds of snowy nights and winter twilight in their “Winter’s Night
 ” concert at 4 pm on Sunday\, December 6\, in downtown Petaluma. The con
 cert features Leo Delibes’ lovely Messe Breve and the spirited “Boa No
 ite\, Minha Gente\,” a festive Brazilian song for women inspired by the 
 “baiana” celebration. This is the Chorus’ first season singing in ou
 r new home\, the historic Hall of the Above at 199 N. Petaluma Blvd. (the 
 corner of East Washington and Petaluma Boulevard). We can’t wait for you
  to hear the sound of the full choir performing in the great acoustics of 
 this beautiful space! See you there. Tickets are available via Square Paym
 ent system (link included here) or at the door. Tickets $20 General Admiss
 ion $15 Students Sadie Sonntag\, Artistic Director Lori Sikorski\, Accompa
 nist
URL:https://business.petalumachamber.com/events/details/winter-s-night-win
 ter-choral-concert
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
